    summary: "Network mapper for host discovery, port scanning, and service detection.",
    content: "# Nmap Scanning\n\nNmap (Network Mapper) is a free and open-source utility for network discovery and security auditing. It sends crafted packets and analyzes responses to determine which hosts are up, what services they run, and what operating systems they use.\n\n## Common Scan Types\n\n- -sS (SYN scan, default if root): half-open scan, sends SYN, waits for SYN/ACK (open) or RST (closed). Stealthy because no full TCP connection is established.\n- -sT (TCP connect scan): completes the 3-way handshake. Works without root, but is noisy and logged by services.\n- -sU (UDP scan): slow because UDP is connectionless; uses ICMP port-unreachable to infer closed ports.\n- -sV (version detection): probes open ports to identify service and version.\n- -O (OS detection): uses TCP/IP fingerprinting.\n- -A (aggressive): combines OS, version, script scanning, and traceroute.\n- -sn (ping scan): host discovery only, no port scan.\n\n## Useful Flags\n\n- -p- : scan all 65535 TCP ports.\n- -p 1-1000 : scan a port range.\n- --top-ports 100 : scan the 100 most common ports.\n- -T4 : timing template (0=paranoid, 5=insane). T4 is a good default for LAN.\n- --script vuln : run the vuln category of NSE scripts.\n- -oA basename : output in normal, XML, and grepable formats.\n\n## Examples\n\nScan a single host for common ports and versions:\n\n    nmap -sV 192.168.1.10\n\nFast scan of a /24 subnet, host discovery only:\n\n    nmap -sn 192.168.1.0/24\n\nAggressive scan with NSE scripts:\n\n    nmap -A -T4 --script default,vuln 10.0.0.5\n\n## Defense and Detection\n\n- Rate-limit or firewall ICMP and SYN from untrusted sources.\n- Use an IDS (Snort, Suricata) with Nmap signatures.\n- Deploy a port-knocking daemon or SPA (Single Packet Authorization) to hide services from scanners.\n\n## Ethics\n\nOnly scan networks you own or have explicit written permission to test. Unauthorized port scanning is illegal in many jurisdictions.",
